######## 71. The agent imports env files, and the human approves it in the app

-- the app is closed: the human is asked to open it, and an onboard run anyway imports nothing

$ kagebunshin next inbox ledger
2 checkouts
  $T/work/inbox: this checkout is in no kagebunshin project
  $T/work/ledger: this checkout is in no kagebunshin project
waiting on the human; tell them:
  - Please open the kagebunshin app (`kagebunshin app`) and say when it is open: I then move the values of the env files of $T/work/inbox, $T/work/ledger into kagebunshin, and you approve it in the app's window with the store passphrase. Or run `kagebunshin onboard $T/work/inbox $T/work/ledger` in a terminal yourself; it asks for the passphrase there.
nothing more you can do until the human has done the above

$ kagebunshin onboard inbox ledger
onboarding 2 apps in 2 checkouts: 2 env files to import
  $T/work/inbox: import .env into new project inbox
  $T/work/ledger: import .env into new project ledger
kagebunshin: importing 2 env files takes the local store's passphrase, which a person types: in the app when this runs with no terminal, and the app is not open; nothing was imported
hint: once the app is open, run this again: the app's window lists what is imported and takes the passphrase. In a terminal this asks for the passphrase itself
ask the human: open the app (`kagebunshin app`), so the import into the local store can be approved there
[exit 5]

$ kagebunshin --json onboard inbox ledger
onboarding 2 apps in 2 checkouts: 2 env files to import
  $T/work/inbox: import .env into new project inbox
  $T/work/ledger: import .env into new project ledger
{"code":"no_app","message":"importing 2 env files takes the local store's passphrase, which a person types: in the app when this runs with no terminal, and the app is not open; nothing was imported","hint":"once the app is open, run this again: the app's window lists what is imported and takes the passphrase. In a terminal this asks for the passphrase itself","who":"human","tell":"open the app (`kagebunshin app`), so the import into the local store can be approved there"}
[exit 5]

